UNANIMOUS YELLOW — honest, well-controlled experiment sitting at documented-mechanism altitude with a thin but real framing delta. Aggregation by stress-test:

STRESS-TEST A (issue-tracker collision): CLEARED. All five reviewers searched independently (novelty_killer cites pandas #44099, #22143; systems_reviewer searched "cat.codes parquet", "cat.codes across files", "cat.codes machine learning"). The closest hits are concat/category-ordering issues, NOT the cross-shard .cat.codes-as-ML-feature-contract framing. No triaged issue, no merged fix. This is NOT a CLAIM-0066 repeat — no RED trigger from the issue tracker. Anti-hallucination rule honored: collision absence verified across ≥2 independent reviewer searches with cited URLs.

STRESS-TEST B (altitude — non-obvious coupling vs. documented folklore): THIS IS THE GATING QUESTION and the reason for YELLOW, not GREEN. Four of five reviewers converge on the same diagnosis: the MECHANISM (astype('category') sorts over observed values; codes are positional in the sorted categories array) is fully documented in pandas docs (novelty_killer cites the Categorical.codes API reference). The NON-PORTABILITY circulates as community folklore (novelty_killer: SO Q54731396; systems_reviewer: CategoricalDtype docs prescribe the fix). Theory_skeptic sharpens this: "the cross-shard mismatch follows by definition of 'sort'" — nothing theoretically surprising, and tree-R2 collapse on scrambled integer codes is elementary splitter theory. The claim's defense (A emits strings only; B's per-file docs don't fire the cross-shard alarm; B never fits an encoder) is coherent but thin — it amounts to "the docs don't warn about THIS specific downstream consequence," which is a documentation-coverage gap, not a mechanism discovery. Evaluation_prosecutor delivers the strongest structural blow: the multi-shard pipeline is a STRAWMAN because it omits standard schema management (Global CategoricalDtype, OrdinalEncoder) that any Dask/multi-file practitioner would apply. This objection is unrebutted and must be addressed at L1 with the mandatory baselines.

STRESS-TEST C (not standard leakage): CLEARED. Product_realist and the packet itself establish the distinction: no fitted estimator, contract set by storage cast, not fit-transform. Kapoor-Narayanan 2023 is orthogonal (within-dataset train/test contamination). This distinction is real and sufficient.

WHY NOT GREEN: I cannot emit GREEN when (i) the mechanism is documented and the non-portability is folklore (novelty_killer, theory_skeptic — unrebutted), (ii) the evaluation_prosecutor's strawman/mandatory-baseline objection is unrebutted (standard practices trivially prevent the failure), and (iii) the sociotechnical load-bearing assumption (real consumers use raw .cat.codes cross-shard) is asserted but unmeasured (theory_skeptic + product_realist convergence). GREEN requires that these are addressed, not merely acknowledged.

WHY NOT RED: (i) No issue-tracker collision — the CLAIM-0066 RED trigger is definitively absent. (ii) The framing delta is real: no pandas doc, SO answer, or issue explicitly warns that astype('category').cat.codes produces UNSTABLE ML FEATURE IDS across separately-cast shards — the consequence framing + the exact f=0 null boundary + the monotonic dose-response is a genuine empirical composition that was not found pre-existing. (iii) The experiment is exceptionally clean: pandas 3.0.3 (current), composition a/b/c verified with probes, realistic SNR (R2~0.78, not inflated), RF cross-check, 12-seed stability, two mechanistically distinct arms, all could-fail audits clean. Honest, non-rigged L0 work deserves advancement to L1, not termination.

DISAGREEMENT RESOLUTION: No reviewer-to-reviewer disagreement exists (all YELLOW). The five reviewers' concerns are COMPLEMENTARY, not conflicting: novelty_killer establishes the thin framing delta; systems_reviewer confirms no shipping-system collision; evaluation_prosecutor identifies the mandatory baselines; theory_skeptic bounds what is and isn't surprising; product_realist scopes the real-world niche. All five concerns are incorporated into the REQUIRED_EVIDENCE and MANDATORY_BASELINES lists for L1.

DECISION: Advance to L1 with the five required evidence items and three mandatory baselines pre-registered. The L1 verdict hinges on: does the Global-CategoricalDtype baseline zero deltaR2 (expected yes — confirming this is a missing-practice issue, not a framework defect)? Does a real consumer pattern exist in the wild? Does the f-distribution on real partitioned data fall in the hazardous band? If L1 answers these, the claim's altitude resolves to either a valuable "missing-practice awareness" contribution (GREEN at that reduced altitude) or a strawman (RED). Current altitude: framing-composition-over-documented-mechanism.

